      "title": "Third-Party Dependency Failures and Vendor API Issues",
      "content_summary": "General guidance for diagnosing and resolving issues caused by downstream service degradation, expired credentials, or vendor API deprecations affecting Chat Widget and Mobile App notifications.",
      "content_body": "When notification failures or timeouts occur in the Chat Widget or Mobile App, first check the vendor's status page for active incidents. If the status is green but errors persist, inspect logs for upstream dependency timeouts or authentication errors indicating an expired API key. For version conflicts or deprecated endpoints, review recent vendor release notes and update client dependencies accordingly. Credential rotation is required if authentication failures are confirmed; otherwise, engage the vendor support team for deeper remediation of service-level failures."
